doctype html
html(lang="en")
  head
    title Paramoji - Parametric Emoji
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='style.css')
    meta(charset="utf-8")
    meta(name="description" content="A parametric emoji that can be parameterized with five continuous dimensions. It visualizes and unifies dimensional and categorical emotional models.")
  h1#paramoji Paramoji
  h2#what-is-a-paramoji What is a paramoji
  p
    | A paramoji is a parametric emoji. It renders facial expressions
    | from five continuous parameters. It can be used to visualize manually selected, automatically detected or
    | computationally generated emotions with accuracy and with arbitrary nuances.
    | The resulting emoji style icons are expressive, exaggerated and playful. Their emotional content
    | can be easily recognized by humans.
  p(style="text-align:center")
    a(href='https://paramoji.org/editor.html')
      button(style="width:300px") Try out your own
  h2#what-are-the-available-dimensions-of-the-paramoji What are the available dimensions of the paramoji
  p The paramoji renders from the following meaningful parameters:
  ol
    li
      em Valence
      |  is the axis from bad to good, misery to pleasure, disagreement to agrement.
    li
      em Arousal
      |  is the axis from calm to aroused, inactive to active, sleepy to alarmed.
    li
      em Dominance
      |  is the axis from weakness to strength, fear to anger, submission to dominance.
    li
      em Contempt
      |  is the axis from neutral to smug, vain, disdainful and contempt.
    li
      em Control
      |  is the axis from uncontrolled to controlled, expressed to suppressed.
  p
    | With these dimensions the paramoji is able to express the emotional dimensions of the
    | <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235361517_A_Circumplex_Model_of_Affect"> Circumplex model of affect</a>
    | and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PAD_emotional_state_model">PAD model</a>
    | of emotional states.
  h2#what-emotions-can-be-represented-with-the-paramoji What emotions can be represented with the paramoji
  p
    | The paramoji parameterizes facial expressions with a wide variety of emotional expressions.
    | They can represent the seven
    | <a href="https://www.paulekman.com/universal-emotions">universal emotions defined by Paul Ekman</a>
    | with reasonable completeness. Here are the author's pick for those emotions. You can click the image
    | to create your own variations of those expressions.
  .ekman-table
    .table-head Normal
    .table-head Happy
    .table-head Sad
    .table-head Surpriseed
    a.onhover(href='https://paramoji.org/editor.html?v=59&a1=35&a2=17&d=50&c=0')
